codex
## 1. Ticket 17 checklist

- **A1 — Partially earned.** Empty/static-load-type cases are guarded and tested. However, validation prefers the live exercise load type after snapshot freeze; a weighted snapshot can later accept reps-only as bodyweight and recreate `— × reps` history. [WorkoutSession.swift:402](</Users/ericlee06/orca/projects/Health App/WorkoutTracker/Domain/WorkoutSession.swift:402>)
- **A2 — Partially earned.** Ordinary empty, draft-only, stray, and minimized-then-resumed finishes delete safely; the confirmation wrapper avoids a deleted sheet subject. Empty template workouts remain destructive; see Critical finding.
- **B1 — Earned.** Values copy from the last completed set while `completedAt` remains nil; cross-workout prefill is prevented from overwriting carry-forward. Logging still requires a tap.
- **B2 — Earned.** Scratch-workout Finish finishes immediately; D18 remains for templated drift.
- **B3 — Earned.** Focused numeric fields expose Done and commit through the existing end-edit boundary.
- **C1 — Earned.** Minimize clears only presentation state; the persisted active workout receives a resume row.
- **C2 — Partially earned.** The receipt appears, but “View in History” only selects the History tab—it does not open the workout just logged. [RootView.swift:56](</Users/ericlee06/orca/projects/Health App/WorkoutTracker/App/RootView.swift:56>)
- **D1 — Partially earned.** Selection persists and no-gym machine logging is explained. Archiving the currently selected gym during the same app lifetime leaves the stale `@State` gym selected, allowing a workout at an archived gym.
- **D2 — Earned.** Gym city/unit and machine unit/label are editable; model correction remains in the D10-scoped flow.
- **D3 — Earned.** Model selection supplies `modelName` and immediately enables Add.
- **E1 — Partially earned.** Exercise-derived titles use snapshot names, but template titles use the live template table and gym rendering has a live fallback, violating D10/D23.
- **E2 — Earned.** Singular/plural handling covers exercises and sets.
- **E3 — Earned.** Durations below 60 seconds render in seconds.
- **E4 — Earned.** The unit badge now follows the stats in the same row.
- **E5 — Partially earned.** The control is now a named, accessible menu, but its unchanged visual label is still just `1`/`2`; there is no visible menu affordance.

## 2. New findings by severity

### Critical

- **An empty template workout can erase its template.** Start from a non-empty template, complete nothing, Finish, then choose Update Template or Update Both. Drift application deletes every template item before `finish()` discards the empty workout. The receipt then says nothing was saved although the reusable template was destroyed. [TemplateDrift.swift:135](</Users/ericlee06/orca/projects/Health App/WorkoutTracker/Domain/TemplateDrift.swift:135>) [TemplateDrift.swift:162](</Users/ericlee06/orca/projects/Health App/WorkoutTracker/Domain/TemplateDrift.swift:162>)

### Important

- **History titles violate snapshot-keyed history.** Renaming or deleting a template retitles old workouts because `HistoryView` reads current `WorkoutTemplate.name`. The gym fallback similarly reads `gym?.name`. [HistoryView.swift:11](</Users/ericlee06/orca/projects/Health App/WorkoutTracker/Features/History/HistoryView.swift:11>) [HistoryRendering.swift:135](</Users/ericlee06/orca/projects/Health App/WorkoutTracker/Domain/HistoryRendering.swift:135>)
- **A frozen entry still validates using live load type.** Catalog reconciliation can change a live exercise while an active workout is recovered; subsequent sets then use different requirements from the frozen snapshot under which they enter history. [ExerciseEntryCard.swift:27](</Users/ericlee06/orca/projects/Health App/WorkoutTracker/Features/ActiveWorkout/ExerciseEntryCard.swift:27>)
- **The post-finish “link” does not link to the workout.** It merely opens the history list; `HistoryView.path` is never populated.
- **History title deduplication uses names rather than snapshot exercise IDs.** Two distinct exercises sharing a display name collapse into one, producing an indistinguishable title. [HistoryRendering.swift:68](</Users/ericlee06/orca/projects/Health App/WorkoutTracker/Domain/HistoryRendering.swift:68>)

### Minor

- **The UI and domain disagree on weight validity.** `parseWeight` treats negative/NaN/infinite values as present, enabling completion; `StoredWeight` then rejects them and the tap silently does nothing. [ExerciseEntryCard.swift:353](</Users/ericlee06/orca/projects/Health App/WorkoutTracker/Features/ActiveWorkout/ExerciseEntryCard.swift:353>)
- **Post-finish summary uses the live gym relationship**, despite having `historyGymName` available. [WorkoutFinishedSheet.swift:125](</Users/ericlee06/orca/projects/Health App/WorkoutTracker/Features/ActiveWorkout/WorkoutFinishedSheet.swift:125>)
- **Test adjustments did not weaken their original assertions.** Required weight/reps were added without changing the tested memory, drift, freeze, cancel, or auto-finish behavior; the A1/A2/B1 regressions would fail against the old code. Missing coverage: empty-template drift, template rename/delete, direct History navigation, invalid weight UI, B3, and E5 discoverability.
- **Runtime verification was not reproduced.** CoreSimulatorService has no available runtime in this environment; both `xcodebuild test` and `build-for-testing` stopped in simulator/asset tooling before tests ran.

## 3. Overall verdict

**No—unsafe to dogfood until the empty-template data-loss path and D23 history/load-type violations are fixed.**
